resources.string:
Custom button guide

Triggers:
1. Short press: runs function run() in the Button JS.
2. Long press: opens the login entry. The login UI uses loginUi; tapping the login button runs function login() in loginUrl.
3. If loginUi is empty but loginUrl defines function login(), a long press runs the login logic directly.

Available to run() on short press:
- book: the current book. Common fields: book.name, book.author, book.bookUrl, book.origin, book.originName, book.kind, book.customTag, book.coverUrl, book.intro, book.latestChapterTitle, book.totalChapterNum, book.durChapterIndex.
- chapter: the current chapter. Common fields: chapter.title, chapter.index, chapter.url, chapter.baseUrl, chapter.bookUrl, chapter.tag, chapter.wordCount, chapter.variable.
- content / src / result: the current chapter text; all three are identical.
- title: the current chapter title; same as chapter.title.
- baseUrl: the request URL of the current chapter; prefers the chapter\'s absolute URL.
- bookSource / readSource: the book source being read; may be null.
- button: the current custom button. Common fields: button.id, button.name, button.loginUrl, button.loginUi, button.jsLib, button.timeoutMillisecond.
- source: the current button source. Common methods: source.getKey(), source.getTag(), source.get(key), source.put(key,value), source.getVariable(), source.putVariable(value), source.login().
- java: reading page helper. Common methods: java.copyText(text), java.showBrowser(url, html), java.refreshBookInfo(), java.refreshBookToc(), java.refreshContent().
- cache / cookie: cache and cookie helpers.

Available to long-press login:
- book: the current book.
- chapter: the current chapter.
- result: the login form data map, e.g. result.bookName.
- isLongClick: whether a long press triggered it.
- source / java / cache / cookie: same as above.

Short press test, put this in Button JS:
function run() {
    var info = {
        bookName: book ? book.name : "",
        author: book ? book.author : "",
        bookUrl: book ? book.bookUrl : "",
        originName: book ? book.originName : "",
        chapterTitle: chapter ? chapter.title : title,
        chapterIndex: chapter ? chapter.index : -1,
        chapterUrl: chapter ? chapter.url : "",
        baseUrl: baseUrl,
        buttonId: button ? button.id : "",
        buttonName: button ? button.name : "",
        sourceKey: source.getKey(),
        sourceTag: source.getTag(),
        textLength: (content || "").length
    };
    var text = JSON.stringify(info, null, 2);
    java.copyText(text);
    java.showBrowser(baseUrl || "about:blank", "<pre style=\'white-space:pre-wrap\'>" + text + "</pre>");
    return text;
}

Long press login test:
1. loginUi:
@js:
JSON.stringify([
    {name:"bookName", type:"text", viewName:"Title", default:book ? book.name : ""},
    {name:"chapterTitle", type:"text", viewName:"Chapter", default:chapter ? chapter.title : ""},
    {name:"copyInfo", type:"button", viewName:"Copy login info", action:"java.copyText(JSON.stringify({bookName:book?book.name:\'\', chapterTitle:chapter?chapter.title:\'\', form:result, isLongClick:isLongClick}, null, 2))"}
])

2. loginUrl:
function login() {
    var info = {
        bookName: book ? book.name : "",
        chapterTitle: chapter ? chapter.title : "",
        form: result,
        isLongClick: isLongClick
    };
    var text = JSON.stringify(info, null, 2);
    source.put("lastLoginTest", text);
    java.copyText(text);
    return true;
}

Note: custom buttons are meant for reading and helper actions; do not modify the chapter text directly.
